-  {{ $result = "even" }}
-{{ else }}
-  {{ $result = "odd" }}
+  {{ return "even" }}
 {{ end }}
-{{ return $result }}
+{{ return "odd" }}
 ```
 
-> [!NOTE]
-> The construct below is incorrect; it contains more than one `return` statement.
+In a _partial_ template, a `return` statement without a value stops execution and returns the output rendered so far. In any other template, it stops rendering, keeping the output rendered so far, and any value is discarded.
 
-```go-html-template {file="layouts/_partials/do-not-do-this.html"}
-{{ if math.ModBool . 2 }}
-  {{ return "even" }}
-{{ else }}
-  {{ return "odd" }}
-{{ end }}
-```
+Within a template invoked with the [`template`] or [`block`] statements, `return` terminates that template only.
 
 [`text/template`]: https://pkg.go.dev/text/template
+[`template`]: /functions/go-template/template/
+[`block`]: /functions/go-template/block/
